From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bottlerocket Builder <builder@bottlerocket.aws>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vendor: add explicit modules.txt entry for go-proxyproto

The EKS distro v1.34.9 source adds github.com/pires/go-proxyproto as an
explicit require in staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/go.mod but does not
re-run `go work vendor`, leaving vendor/modules.txt without the
corresponding entry. This breaks hermetic (vendor-mode) builds with:

  inconsistent vendoring: github.com/pires/go-proxyproto ... is
  explicitly required in go.mod, but not marked as explicit in
  vendor/modules.txt

The module is not imported by any package in the tree, so only the
module-level explicit annotation is required (no vendored package
paths). This matches what `go work vendor` would generate.
---
 vendor/modules.txt | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vendor/modules.txt b/vendor/modules.txt
index 5339335..84602f7 100644
--- a/vendor/modules.txt
+++ b/vendor/modules.txt
@@ -484,6 +484,8 @@ github.com/opencontainers/selinux/pkg/pwalkdir
 # github.com/peterbourgon/diskv v2.0.1+incompatible
 ## explicit
 github.com/peterbourgon/diskv
+# github.com/pires/go-proxyproto v0.7.1-0.20240628150027-b718e7ce4964
+## explicit; go 1.18
 # github.com/pkg/errors v0.9.1
 ## explicit
 github.com/pkg/errors
--
2.52.0
